89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Don't design to deceive. If a client asks me to make something look eco-friendly when it isn't, or to hide a "cancel" button, I won't do it. Dark patterns are a choice, and so is refusing them. Design can build trust or break it. I want to build it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 58 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [217 0 R 0]
/K [6]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Representation isn't decoration. I live on the unceded territories of the Musqueam, Squamish, and Tsleil-Waututh peoples, and I come from Hokkaido, the ancestral homeland of the Ainu people. Both communities remind me that representation carries real weight. When I create work that features people, I always want to ask: would they feel respected, or used?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 58 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [218 0 R 0]
/K [8]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Protect the craft, mine and everyone else's. My mom was a fashion designer. I grew up watching her work, and she made so many pieces that literally coloured my life. So when I see design theft, or AI trained on stolen work, it hits differently. I want to credit people, pay fair rates, and never undercut the designers around me.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 58 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [219 0 R 0]
/K [10]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Keep asking questions. My thinking about design ethics started somewhere really basic, like "don't plagiarize" or "just be a decent human being." I never got to put it into my own words. Now I do. The habit of asking who benefits, who gets left out, and what the real cost is, that is actually the whole point.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 58 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
/A [220 0 R 0]
/K [12]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 58 0 R
/E (Know when to say no. Spec work, harmful briefs, clients who don't respect the process. Saying no is a skill and a professional one. I don't contribute to free work either. Knowing my own value is also a way of supporting every other creator who deserves to be paid fairly.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
