/T (Tension 01: AI efficiency vs. creative authenticity)
/E (Tension 01: AI efficiency vs. creative authenticity)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (I use AI to brainstorm ideas, write code, and speed up my workflow. But there is a real question underneath all of that: at what point does relying on AI start to hollow out my own skills? And what do I owe to the artists whose work trained these models? I don't have a clean answer yet. But I think the minimum I can do is be transparent about when and how I use AI, and keep pushing myself to develop my own eye.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 59 0 R
/T (Tension 02: Client wants vs. audience harm)
/E (Tension 02: Client wants vs. audience harm)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (In brand and marketing design, you will eventually receive a brief that asks you to exaggerate. The client pays you. The audience doesn't. This is the tension I worry about most, because it is subtle. Nobody hands you a brief that says "please deceive people." It usually just looks like "make it more exciting" or "soften the negative." I want to be the designer who names that tension out loud, even when it's a bit uncomfortable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
